# greetd's PAM service. It ships its own file to /etc/pam.d/greetd, which this
# image does not have for the reason system-auth beside it records.
#
# Without this, greetd starts and looks healthy -- measured, it reported active
# and running -- while every authentication through it fails. That is the same
# shape as the rest of this project's fail-open findings: the service is up, so
# nothing looks wrong, and the mechanism it exists for does not work.
auth        include                                      system-auth
account     include                                      system-auth
password    include                                      system-auth
session     include                                      system-auth
